.TH EUCLID-CLI-ESM-VERIFY-OBJECTS 1 "November 2026" "euclid-cli 2.1.3" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-esm-verify-objects \- find objects whose file on disk does not match their record
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli esm verify-objects
(\fB\-\-bucket\fR|\fB\-b\fR \fIBUCKET\fR | \fB\-\-all\-buckets\fR|\fB\-a\fR)
[\fB\-\-after\-key\fR|\fB\-k\fR \fIKEY\fR]
[\fB\-\-page\-size\fR|\fB\-s\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-\-one\-page\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
An object is two things: a record in the database \- its key, size,
checksum and status \- and a file under ESM's data directory holding its
bytes. This command finds the objects where the two disagree.
.PP
That is what a machine going down leaves behind. The record is written
by the database, which keeps it; the file's bytes may still have been in
memory when the power went, and come back empty, cut short, or not at
all. Reading such an object fails \- or, before ESM checked, returned the
empty file as though it were the object, which is how an image service
came to be handed an empty image. ESM now forces every file onto the disk
before it records it, so a crash cannot leave new ones; this finds the
ones left before.
.PP
Each object is judged by size, not content: one
.BR stat (2)
per object, and a read of the header for an encrypted one. It is quick,
and never reads the bytes \- so a file of the right length with the wrong
bytes in it is the one case it does not catch.
.PP
Skipped, and counted as such: objects still being uploaded, archived ones
(their bytes are in the month's archive, not a file), and directory
markers.
.SH PROBLEMS
.TP
.B missing
There is no file.
.TP
.B empty
The file has no bytes, the object does.
.TP
.B short
The file has fewer bytes than it should.
.TP
.B long
The file has more bytes than it should.
.TP
.B mismatch
An encrypted file whose header records a different length than the
object does.
.TP
.B unreadable
The file cannot be read, or is not an encrypted object although the
record says it is;
.I detail
says which.
.PP
For an encrypted object the size it should have is computed from its own
header: the header, the plaintext, and 28 bytes per 64 KiB frame.
.SH WHAT TO DO WITH WHAT IT FINDS
The bytes are gone; there is nothing in ESM to repair them from. Delete
the object with
.BR euclid-cli-esm-delete-objects (1)
\- so that a reader gets "not found" rather than a failure it will retry
for ever \- and have whatever sent it send it again.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-bucket " " \fIBUCKET\fR
The bucket to check, by name or ERN.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-all\-buckets
Every bucket of the session's namespace, one after the other.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-after\-key " " \fIKEY\fR
Start after this key \- where an interrupted run's progress said it was.
Only with
.BR \-\-bucket .
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-page\-size " " \fIN\fR
Objects looked at per request, from 1 to 100000. Default 10000.
.TP
.B \-\-one\-page
Check one page and print it as ESM answered it, with
.I nextKey
\- the key the next page starts after, empty at the end of the bucket.
.SH OUTPUT
Progress goes to standard error, one line per page, ending with the key
the next page starts after \- what
.B \-\-after\-key
takes to resume. The report goes to standard output once the walk is
done:
.RS
.nf
{"checked": 120000, "problems": 1, "buckets": [
  {"bucketErn": "...:bucket:file-delivery", "checked": 120000, "skipped": 0,
   "problems": [{"key": "DLI145/...jpg", "ern": "...", "problem": "empty",
                 "recordedSize": 281861, "fileSize": 0, "expectedFileSize": 281861,
                 "internalName": "d35f0895-...", "created": "2026-10-30T03:44:44Z"}]}]}
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Every object checked is whole.
.TP
.B 2
Problems were found; they are in the report.
.TP
.B 1
The check could not be run: not authenticated, no such bucket, no access
to it, or a request failed.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
# One bucket
euclid-cli esm verify-objects --bucket file-delivery > file-delivery-check.json

# Everything, after a crash
euclid-cli esm verify-objects --all-buckets > check.json

# Resume where an interrupted run stopped
euclid-cli esm verify-objects --bucket file-delivery --after-key "DLI145/9783170359529_COVER_IMAGE_30102026044444425.jpg"
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-esm (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-count-objects (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-delete-objects (1)
